ssessing the application of bolding and bullets • making sure the three dash dividers are present • The focus is precise adherence to every directive.\n\n\n**Implementing Text Conversion**\n\nI'm presently focused on a\n<truncated 4105 bytes>\ns remains on accurate text transformation and enhanced clarity.\n\n\n**Converting List Content**\n\nI'm currently focused on converting the list content related to the \"Numerical Rating Scale (NRS)\" to match the specified format. I'm removing all punctuation and replacing hyphens with spaces. I'm applying bullets to the list items and making sure the formatting of the text is correct. I am ensuring that the information is easily understood.\n\n\n**Transforming Assessment Details**\n\nI'm now transforming assessment details for accuracy • I've converted \"McGill's Modified Questionnaire\" to the correct bolding, bullet, and dash format. I'm ensuring all the word descriptors are now correctly bulleted with appropriate spaces where hyphens once were. Clarity and accuracy are the core goals during this transform.\n\n\n**Converting Descriptor Data**\n\nI'm now converting the descriptor data, starting with \"Scoring System.\" I've bulleted the main section, removed the asterisks, and converted the \"0 = None\" format to a bulleted list with the same meaning. I am ensuring that the sub-items are properly bulleted, and maintaining clarity in the transformation. I am focusing on precision, and I've also done the same for \"Indices Documented.\"\n\n\n**Refining Term Conversions**\n\nI'm now refining the format conversions for specific terms and phrases within the provided text. I've successfully replaced all remaining instances of hyphens with spaces and dealt with any and all remaining formatting issues. I've also processed abbreviations such as VAS, NRS. My focus is now on ensuring accuracy in the new format.\n\n\n**Finalizing Numerical Data**\n\nI'm now finalizing the numerical data conversions, using the \"Numerical Rating Scale (